{
  "v": 2,
  "order": 510,
  "label": "Decision Matrix",
  "group": "Worked examples",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "noteIntro",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 355,
      "y": 1805,
      "init": {
        "label": "Decision Matrix",
        "body": "# Weighted scoring, ranked\nA **Decision Matrix** scores each laptop against the criteria and ranks them, best first.\n\nThe **Weights** table says how much each criterion counts. A negative weight means lower is better, like Price. Change a weight and the ranking moves.\n\nThe screen scores come from a **Note** below, joined in by laptop name, and a **Report** at the end writes up the result.",
        "color": "violet",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scores",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 841,
      "y": 1843,
      "init": {
        "label": "Score table",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Laptop\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"ProBook\",\"UltraSlim\",\"PowerLifter\",\"ValueBook\"]},{\"name\":\"Performance\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[9,6,10,4]},{\"name\":\"Battery\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[6,9,5,7]},{\"name\":\"Price\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[1800,1400,2200,700]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteScreen",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 683,
      "y": 2143,
      "init": {
        "label": "Screen scores",
        "body": "---\nscreen:\n  - Laptop: ProBook\n    Screen: 8\n  - Laptop: UltraSlim\n    Screen: 9\n  - Laptop: PowerLifter\n    Screen: 7\n  - Laptop: ValueBook\n    Screen: 5\n---\n### Screen scores\nProBook 8: 4K panel with an anti-glare coating. UltraSlim 9: brightest of the four. PowerLifter 7: sharp but reflective. ValueBook 5: a review flagged weak brightness.\n\nThe list at the top of this note is a table of its own, so each score stays with its laptop however the main table is sorted.",
        "color": "amber",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 250
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "join",
      "type": "JoinNode",
      "x": 1192,
      "y": 2035,
      "init": {
        "label": "Join on Laptop",
        "how": "left"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "leftKey": "Laptop",
        "rightKey": "Laptop"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dm",
      "type": "DecisionMatrixNode",
      "x": 1976,
      "y": 721,
      "init": {
        "label": "Decision Matrix",
        "normalize": "max",
        "detail": "breakdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "weights",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 1647,
      "y": 713,
      "init": {
        "label": "Weights",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Criterion\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"Performance\",\"Battery\",\"Screen\",\"Price\"]},{\"name\":\"Weight\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[3,2,1,-2]},{\"name\":\"Norm\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"\",\"\",\"\",\"Rank\"]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteDM",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 1749,
      "y": 1234,
      "init": {
        "label": "Mixed scales, one range",
        "body": "Price is in **dollars**; the rest are out of **10**. Scored raw, the dollar column would swamp everything, so each column is first squeezed onto the same footing; then only the **weights** decide influence.\n\n**÷Max** divides a column by its biggest value, so each tops out at 1. **Rank** keeps only the order: $2,200 counts as “most expensive”, not as 2,200 of anything. Price uses Rank; the rest follow the ÷Max default.\n\n**Breakdown** is on: each criterion column is its **signed contribution**, and the contributions sum to the Score. Price shows negative, the penalty it is.",
        "color": "green",
        "width": 370,
        "height": 280
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "select",
      "type": "ColumnsNode",
      "x": 2456,
      "y": 513,
      "init": {
        "label": "Keep Laptop · Score"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "columns": "Laptop,Score"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chart",
      "type": "ChartNode",
      "x": 2785,
      "y": 521,
      "init": {
        "label": "Podium",
        "op": "bar"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "options": "title=Weighted score;xlabel=Score"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteChart",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 2404,
      "y": 135,
      "init": {
        "label": "The podium is a chart",
        "body": "The ranking is already the table. For the podium, **Select Columns** keeps `Laptop · Score`, and a two-column frame into **Chart** draws labeled bars: the first column names them, the second sets the lengths.",
        "color": "vermilion",
        "width": 320,
        "height": 160
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "winner",
      "type": "ListIndexNode",
      "x": 2629,
      "y": 900,
      "init": {
        "label": "Winner"
      },
      "literals": {
        "index": 1,
        "column": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "report",
      "type": "ReportNode",
      "x": 3174,
      "y": 472,
      "init": {
        "label": "Decision memo",
        "body": "# Laptop pick\n\nWith the weights on the canvas, the matrix picks {{ winner | highlight }}.\n\n{{ podium }}\n\nBehind the bars, each criterion column is a signed contribution; the contributions sum to the Score, and Price counts against:\n\n{{ ranking }}\n\nThe podium in words: the ranking sorted by rank and sliced to three:\n\n{% for r in ranking | sort:\"Rank\" | slice:0,3 %}{{ r.Rank }}. **{{ r.Laptop }}** at {{ r.Score | number_format:2 }}\n{% endfor %}\nEvery figure here is wired. Change a weight or a score upstream and the memo follows."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noteSens",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 1744,
      "y": 1977,
      "init": {
        "label": "Sensitivity",
        "body": "# Stress-test the weights\nThe winner depends on the weights picked above. **Sensitivity** re-scores the same laptops under several sets of weights, one per column of the Scenarios table. For each it gives the **Winner**, the **Margin** over the runner-up, and the full **Ranking** to open.\n\n**UltraSlim** wins under Balanced and **PowerLifter** when performance dominates. Under Budget it reads **Tie: UltraSlim, ValueBook** at Margin 0: that pick is fragile, the first two hold.",
        "color": "blue",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 280
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scenarios",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 1647,
      "y": 1610,
      "init": {
        "label": "Weight scenarios",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Criterion\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"Performance\",\"Battery\",\"Screen\",\"Price\"]},{\"name\":\"Balanced\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[3,2,1,-2]},{\"name\":\"Performance-first\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[5,1,1,-1]},{\"name\":\"Budget\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[1,1,1,-5]}]"
      }
    },
